run: /Users/cmatsoukis/Desktop/Apps/experiment-1/runs/bench-watchlist/wl-rename+governor@12000-03
provider: ollama-cloud (glm-5.3)
request: Rename the `watched` field of watchlist items to `seen` everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> movie, watchlist-store, watchlist, movie-detail, search  (Pure data-model rename: WatchItem.watched becomes WatchItem.seen. The type owner (movie) changes the interface; the producer (watchlist-store) and consumers (watchlist, plus movie-detail/search where they read the field) switch references. Store API names (toggleWatched, watchedCount) and user-visible copy are intentionally kept — the request names only the item field, not methods, signals or UI text. Existing-test edits that merely rename the field in fixtures are expected; they will arrive as approval requests next round.)
round 1: owners movie=ok watchlist-store=ok watchlist=rejected movie-detail=ok search=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist, watchlist-store  (The field rename already landed in movie and watchlist-store (manifest shows WatchItem.seen). The round is red only because watchlist's correct submission was rejected over the existing-test rule (its `.watched` read in one spec) and because my watchlist-store acceptance test contains a type-invalid cast. I approve that single test edit — it is exactly the field rename the request calls for — re-issue the watchlist rename instruction, and replace the acceptance test with a type-correct version of the same specification.)
round 2: owners watchlist=ok watchlist-store=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 3: accept  (The rename of the watchlist-item field is complete. `WatchItem` now exposes `seen: boolean` (movie unit), the store creates/flips/persists items under `seen` (watchlist-store), the watchlist template reads were renamed (watchlist), and movie-detail/search confirmed no references to the old field. tsc is clean and all 31 tests pass, including the acceptance tests pinning `seen` on items and the unchanged store method/signal names (`toggleWatched`, `watchedCount`). The request asked to rename the watchlist item field, not the store's method names or UI copy, so those are correctly untouched, and `Movie.watched` is a separate legacy type, not a watchlist item. Nothing remains to change.)

